Z||000000||Gold-86SE||04-28-2000||11:02 PM||||guys, i would have posted this in the technical area, but i have tried for the last 30 minutes and could not get in it for some odd reason.<P>anyway, here is my problem.<P>was driving home tonight, and my car kept dying on me everytime i would come to a stop, finally got it home and checked the codes... a 24... vehicle speed sensor.<P>i had other work to do on the Fiero tonight, so i raised it and while working on the other things discovered a connector loose, hanging on the muffler, needless to say it is somewhat melted.<P>This connector is connected to the speed sensor that goes into the trans, it is two pronged and has the rubber gromet/seal (the seal is like the other seals used on the electrical connections i.e. the map sensor) but where does the freaking thing go?<P>i have a pretty [good] idea that this is causing my problem.  so you can help me it is an 86 2.8 4-spd.<p>[This message has been edited by Gold-86SE (edited 04-28-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||04-29-2000||10:48 AM||||Mr Haynes says "A fault in this circuit should be indicated only when the car is in motion.  Disregard Code 24 if it is set when the drive wheels are not turning.  Check the connection at the ECM. Check the TPS setting"<P>The only thing that I can see in the manual, that "looks" like what you describe is the speedometer gear and speedometer sensor harness. If the wires are broken or melted through, it will be search time for wires back to the ECM.  Not much help.<BR>||||reg||3
